  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "After a face saving draw with Fang Zheng, Wei Wu Shang transmits that Fairy Bi Xia has many admirers and lists Rising Purple Lightning Gu Ting among four further competitors. Three days later disciples of Ancient Soul Sect arrive at Tian Ti mountain with Gu Ting leading them. Learning of the matter between Fairy Bi Xia and Fang Zheng, he sends a challenge. Fang Zheng avoids at first; Gu Ting visits his cave daily for seven days to provoke him, Immortal Crane disciples who go out are defeated, and Ancient Soul Sect’s momentum rises until a crowd blocks Fang Zheng’s cave. When the curses involve Immortal Crane Sect and his master, Fang Zheng walks out; Lord Sky Crane then urges him to fight and defeat Gu Ting. Narration places the fight at the same time as a battle ending on southern border’s San Cha mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        341
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_zheng",
        "char_wei_wu_shang",
        "char_fairy_bi_xia",
        "fac_ancient_soul_sect",
        "loc_tian_ti",
        "fac_immortal_crane_sect",
        "char_lord_sky_crane",
        "loc_san_cha_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "During the Hu Immortal blessed land contest, narration places Fang Zheng, Fairy Bi Xia, Gu Ting, and Wei Wu Shang as only second tier among this generation of elite disciples of the ten great sects, below first-tier disciples such as Feng Jin Huang, Ying Sheng Ji, and Xiao Qi Xing.",
      "chapters": [
        366
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "junior-elite-ranking",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land",
        "char_feng_jin_huang",
        "char_ying_sheng_ji"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On a Heavenly Court list of Gu Immortal seeds with great talent and aptitude, Ancient Soul Sect has Gu Ting beside Immortal Crane Sect’s Sun Yuan Hua, Spirit Butterfly Valley’s Xiao Qi Xing, and Heaven’s Envy Manor’s Wei Wu Shang.",
      "chapters": [
        1970
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "gu-immortal-seed-list",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_sun_yuan_hua",
        "loc_spirit_butterfly_valley",
        "char_xiao_qi_xing",
        "fac_heavens_envy_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Xiao Qi Xing deploys human path soldier Gu, Gu Ting narrows his eyes and asks whether they are soldier Gu, sergeant Gu, and lieutenant Gu. After a victory he warns the group not to be careless, saying those soldiers are only yellow bean divine soldiers, the most basic type.",
      "chapters": [
        2012
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "soldier-tier-warning",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_sergeant_gu",
        "gu_lieutenant_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Fang Di Chang’s fall he says he is more curious about the rewards the sects will give them than about deaths in the painting world.",
      "chapters": [
        2013
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "after-fang-di-chang",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_di_chang"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In a newly added growling beast painting world, when Xiao Qi Xing calls for the group to move against stronger beasts, Chen Da Jiang, Gu Ting, and the rest begin to attack.",
      "chapters": [
        2081
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "growling-beast-painting",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
